			<div class="content" id="post-content-1441938">
									

<p>Fixed your title for you.</p>
<p>Alright, read through most of it, it's 'okay', the tone seems fine (I'm a little tipsy, excuse me if I'm wildly mistaken) and I like the idea. However I must question it's origin and how the Foundation even discovered what it does, improbable things survive fires all the time (no really, it's not that weird), second how did they even become alerted to this and jump to the conclusion that it's anomalous and burns down houses? lastly how did they even find out it burned down houses?</p>
<p>I also must question the Foundation testing anything at all once they found out what it does, just imagine if some poor ass who lived on-site at a Keter facility lit one of these matches &quot;there goes all of the world destroying and super hard to contain monsters, whoops!&quot;</p>
<p>This is one of those cases where I like the idea, the execution is okay, but the finer details on origin mess up my enjoyment.</p>

