<p>Edit: Responding to your questions now. For the testing, I was trying to imply that every one of the subjects was hand-picked by the foundation and informed of SCP-1596's properties beforehand, and not just randomly selected and tested blindly. Admittedly, if any of the agents felt most &quot;at home&quot; at the Foundation, that could cause a problem. But the researchers weren't aware of that until after Test 3, and all testing was suspended immediately afterwards.</p>
