														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1442292">
									

<p>The thought was that the Foundation would have more control over the parameters of the the experiments if the Subject was involved. If you used D-Class Personnel, you'd have to track down their homes and either evacuate them or allow whoever or whatever's inside to burn with the building, both of which would attract a lot of attention and, in the latter case, might be a tad too morally questionable for routine experimentation. It would be easier and more feasible to have the Subject on board as a willing participant who would collaborate with and keep quiet about the testing.</p>
<p>As for the side effect, we're assuming the Foundation already knows the properties of 1596 and is just testing the parameters (distance, whether or not direct contact is needed, etc.) of its effect.</p>

